    "lawCode": "Amd §36, Munic Home R L",
    "lawSection": "Municipal Home Rule Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7344\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the municipal home rule law, in relation to charter\nrevision commissions\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThis bill clearly lays out the process for a charter revision\ncommission to follow. It requires the commission to hold a hearing or\nhearings before it begins its work and again after it presents\npreliminary proposals to the public. It requires that any proposals\nput before the voters be placed on the ballot as separate proposals to\nthe extent practicable. It prevents a commission formed after February\n15 in any given year to place proposals on the ballot in that year,\nunless the commission requests and obtains the consent of the\nlegislative body.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis bill sets forth the process of charter revision in such a way as\nto provide for the public to propose and react to proposals. It\nprovides time for deliberative thinking on the part of all parties,\nboth the members of the commission and the public and a chance to\nfully educate the voters as to any proposals they might vote upon.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nJanuary 1, 2010 and provides for any commission that is in the process\nof deliberations not in compliance with this act is terminated.\n",
